# SS-21 - Intelligent Investor study companion and closed-market research
Workstream ID: SS-21
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/StonksSniper/issues/21
Status: DONE
Milestone: M2
Dependencies: SS-03, SS-05, SS-06

## Purpose
Separate internet technical strategies from a source-linked, original book
companion and help learners apply fundamental concepts to Indian shares.
Make completed-session history usable and understandable on closed-market days.

## Tasks
- [x] Research editions, chapter coverage, historical thresholds and limitations.
- [x] Add distinct technical and book learning sections with ELI15 explanations.
- [x] Add transparent Indian-stock fundamental worksheets and optional real snapshots.
- [x] Distinguish missing evidence, unsupported sectors and current/historical data.
- [x] Verify weekend/holiday fetching, latest-session labels and explicit failures.
- [x] Verify calculations, desktop behavior and actual provider access.
- [x] Update source documentation and register this workstream for synchronization.

## Acceptance criteria
- Existing 27 price strategies and date-range simulations retain their behavior.
- Original summaries cover the 20 main chapters, with sources and edition boundaries;
  no claim of reproducing every example, appendix or later commentary.
- Calculations expose inputs, provenance, units, formulas and uncertainty.
- Missing facts never pass a screen. Industrial balance-sheet tests are not
  presented as bank, insurer or utility eligibility tests.
- Current fundamentals are never silently used in historical backtests.
- Weekend/holiday requests use actual available completed observations without
  fabricated sessions, forward filling or a requirement for an open market.
- Technical verification is separate from human approval and executable publication.

## Completion evidence
- Full offline suite: 269 passed, 4 opt-in live tests skipped, normal exit.
  Ruff lint/format, strict mypy and Git whitespace checks passed.
- Actual Saturday ICICIBANK/NSE history returned 496 observations through
  2026-11-20. Separate real current-fundamental request succeeded.
- Owned native UI diagnostic exercised both real provider workers, all 27
  technical strategies, book classification/calculation and HTML export.
  Chapter/workbook layout inspected at 1366x768 without user-window control.
- Committed ICICIBANK live-provider regression independently passed all strategies.
- Twenty main chapters have original ELI15 notes, practical tasks and source links;
  documentation enumerates historical/local adaptations and research access limits.
  Missing facts remain Unknown; banks/insurers/utilities are not industrial-rated.
- No historical-fundamental backtest, new EXE release, normal-DPI acceptance
  or exhaustive reproduction of all book editions/commentary is claimed.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-21: Started public-source research and inspected existing learning,
  provider, replay and test contracts. Distinguished investing principles from
  daily buy/sell timing rules and latest fundamentals from point-in-time evidence.
- 2026-11-21: Completed source-native companion, pure workbook/scenario arithmetic
  and explicit as-of/weekend disclosures. Fixed a native worker-finalization
  crash by completing native thread cleanup before releasing Python ownership.
  Added regression coverage and actual ICICIBANK closed-market/native checks;
  Yahoo explicitly reported marketState CLOSED. Rejected unsupported numeric
  magnitudes and scenario overflow rather than displaying infinite results.
  Issue #21 and its existing Project item were read back closed-completed/Done.
  Published v0.3.0 is intentionally unchanged.
